        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "14a545ff-6e73-57a4-9fac-9347f0548324",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Whitechapel (TV series)\n- People: Jack the Ripper, Sam Stockman\n- Roles: DC Emerson Kent\n- Places: Whitechapel district of London, UK\n- Events: Whitechapel murders\n- Topics: copycat killings, unsolved murders\n\nFacts:\n- In 1888, Jack the Ripper was an unidentified serial killer generally believed to have been active in the largely impoverished areas in and around the Whitechapel district of London.\n- The Whitechapel murders were a set of eleven unsolved murders of women, and at various points some or all of them were ascribed to Jack the Ripper.\n- The first series of Whitechapel was first broadcast in the UK on 2 February 2009.\n- The first series of Whitechapel depicted the search for a modern copycat killer replicating the murders of Jack the Ripper.\n- Sam Stockman, born in 1982, is a British actor and musician.\n- From 2009 to 2013, Sam Stockman played DC Emerson Kent on the UK crime drama Whitechapel.",
